quivalent to Judo, printed 193), which the book calls the basic style of the Republic''s armed forces and police; the core Martial Arts style is not offered. || RELATED: six, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Espionage''s Tracking is Tracking (people); Wilderness is read as Wilderness Survival, filed under Wilderness in the catalog, which the class also grants. Electrical, Mechanical, Rogue and Science: none, so they are not offered. || SECONDARY: six from the same list without bonuses; the book states no later secondary picks. || MONEY: one month''s salary, 3000 credits; room and board are free. || EQUIPMENT: Kuru or Trooper armor is a choice of the AT-A11 Kuru Street Armor and the AT-A14 Trooper rows. Energy rifle and sidearm of choice are offered from this book''s ArmaTech and H-Brand sets, with four E-clips each. Four grenades of unstated type are offered from this book''s ArmaTech grenade set. The survival kit is stored as its listed contents. Two non-energy weapons of choice are offered from this book''s vibro-blades, swords, tonfa and rail guns. || POWER ARMOR: the book issues Glitter Boy vehicles for field use only and names no model. The Republic fields the traditional USA-G10 (reprinted from the core book on printed 136-137, the catalog''s glitter-boy-power-armor row) alongside the G10A1 Point and G10A2 Hawkeye (printed 138-141), which are not in the catalog yet. None is stored in equipment_starting because none is the pilot''s own; all three are described in the Issued Power Armor section, to be wired to the vehicles tables once the book''s power armor is imported. || CYBERNETICS: 1D4 implants to start, types unstated; prose only."
